identifiers: []
abstract: >-
  Clarifica.ai is a browser extension that brings a full suite of
  accessibility features to the web with all artificial
  intelligence running on-device (Edge AI): extractive question
  answering over the current page, text summarization, image
  captioning, printed-text OCR, speech recognition with live
  captions (bilingual mode), and English-to-Portuguese
  translation, plus three neurodivergent profiles (autism, ADHD,
  dyslexia), color-blindness filters, an Essential Reading mode,
  a real-time WCAG audit panel and profile synchronization.
  Delivered as a WebExtensions package (Manifest V3 for
  Chromium, Manifest V2 for Firefox 115+), it vendors the
  Transformers.js runtime and pins every model to a specific
  Hugging Face commit (SHA) for reproducibility. No text, image
  or audio leaves the user's device: no backend servers, no
  telemetry, no third-party runtime dependencies. Designed and
  tested around screen reader users (NVDA, JAWS) with 199
  unit tests including real model inference and 25 end-to-end
  tests in real Chromium (23 in the standard suite plus 2
  opt-in tests with real AI).
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - edge AI
